{
  "name": "wsapi",
  "description": "WSAPI is a unified interface and abstraction layer between Lua web applications and various web server backends, including CGI, FastCGI, and Xavante. It provides a standardized environment for request/response handling, output buffering, and middleware implementation, drawing architectural inspiration from Ruby's Rack and Python's WSGI while maintaining Lua-specific idioms. The project incorporates C-based FastCGI bindings and specialized launchers to facilitate deployment across heterogeneous UNIX and Windows environments.",
